WEBVTT

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:11.460
Methane Hydrate Mining Site 2

00:01:17.470 --> 00:01:20.430
Methane Hydrate Cartridge

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:38.700
Is this an earthquake?

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.700
What the hell <i>is</i> that?

00:02:43.390 --> 00:02:45.810
Why? Why?

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.980
Why is this happening?

00:03:07.790 --> 00:03:10.960
Why are you after me?!

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:28.560
koreijou kitai wa shinai to sakki kimeta no ni

00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:28.560
I decided that I won't have any more expectations

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:36.360
megakuramu juubyou ga sugireba

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:36.360
But when these dazzling ten seconds pass

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:43.610
sugu yuragu fukidashita yokan

00:03:37.070 --> 00:03:43.610
I already feel like bursting into laughter

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.700
shinkuromanika

00:03:43.610 --> 00:03:45.700
Synchromanica

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.240
itsu no ma ni ka

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.240
Before I know it

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.410
kono koe wa negai no you da

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:50.410
This voice starts to sound like a wish

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:56.710
tanjun ni ikanai mirai ga tokimeki no sumika

00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:56.710
The future isn't simple, but it brings excitement

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:03.220
boku no mimi wa dareka no yume da

00:03:56.710 --> 00:04:03.220
I can hear someone's dream

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:10.180
kotoba ni wa shinain da subete

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:10.180
But I won't say any of it out loud

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.990
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:04:19.530 --> 00:04:22.990
If we understand one another, the gate opens

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.320
shinkuromanika

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.320
Synchromanica

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.450
tsuujiaeba hiraku tobira

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.710
kimi wa ikeru shinkuro

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:39.710
The synchrony of your life

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.550
Galileo DNA

00:04:43.580 --> 00:04:44.550
Ferrari!

00:04:45.110 --> 00:04:46.920
Where is Kazuki Ferrari-kun?

00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:48.280
She said she wasn't feeling well.

00:04:48.280 --> 00:04:49.310
She went to the infirmary.

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:50.620
Again?

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:53.810
She does this every time we have a group activity!

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:10.030
You really don't know how I feel about you, do you?

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:11.960
So, yeah...

00:06:13.010 --> 00:06:15.190
Did you fall asleep?

00:06:17.370 --> 00:06:18.640
I'll take them to court.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:19.430
Huh?

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:26.590
A university, taking your tuition without awarding your credits...

00:06:27.190 --> 00:06:29.280
I'll take them to court!

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:34.030
Uh, hey...

00:06:34.030 --> 00:06:35.910
I feel sick...

00:06:42.350 --> 00:06:46.170
Maybe I should still show up to class...

00:06:48.420 --> 00:06:48.920
Huh?

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:50.430
Wh-What?

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:51.430
Who are you—

00:06:51.830 --> 00:06:54.180
H-Hey, this is the women's room!

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:55.220
Pervert!

00:06:56.090 --> 00:06:57.220
Keep it down.

00:06:57.220 --> 00:07:01.060
Sexual assault is a felony!
You'll get ten years for rape!

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:03.040
Add assault to that and you could get a death sentence!

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.360
We can settle out of court,

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:07.660
but if you don't let me go right now, I <i>will</i> press charges!

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:09.740
I'm a future prosecutor!

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:12.240
You flunked out of law school.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:13.090
Shut up!

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.170
Oh, no!

00:07:39.180 --> 00:07:40.680
Don't make a sound.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.090
Who was that?

00:07:56.090 --> 00:07:58.910
Why? Why was he...

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:09.250
Someone call the police!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:10.710
Ow...

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.760
Wait!

00:08:33.240 --> 00:08:34.740
Stun Gun Launcher...

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.570
I'm sorry.

00:08:51.470 --> 00:08:53.550
I don't understand...

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:58.080
Three attempted abductions on the same day, at the same time.

00:08:58.080 --> 00:09:01.560
I'm thinking these perverts were part of some kind of human trafficking ring.

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:07.100
Galileo sisters, your mother has arrived.

00:09:07.100 --> 00:09:09.760
I really do hate that nickname...

00:09:10.440 --> 00:09:13.280
Do you have any idea who might be behind this?

00:09:13.280 --> 00:09:14.950
How could I possibly?

00:09:15.460 --> 00:09:19.580
Well, these people tried to abduct all three of your daughters simultaneously.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.450
There has to be a reason why.

00:09:21.450 --> 00:09:23.950
And it's <i>your</i> job to figure that out!

00:09:27.310 --> 00:09:28.250
Haa-chan!

00:09:28.250 --> 00:09:29.800
Have you been drinking?

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:31.090
It's the middle of the day.

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.340
What about your classes?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:35.590
Um... Well, how should I—

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.890
Kazuki!

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:40.260
I heard you were skipping class again to hang out in the infirmary.

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:41.930
But group act—

00:09:41.930 --> 00:09:43.010
Hozuki!

00:09:43.010 --> 00:09:46.810
I heard you've been holed up as usual,
barely leaving your room!

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:49.560
Uh, but that's because there was stuff I wanted to do—

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:52.320
Dear God, the three of you...

00:09:52.320 --> 00:09:53.120
Here it is.

00:09:53.120 --> 00:09:54.070
Here she goes.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:54.480
Wait for it.

00:09:54.480 --> 00:09:58.570
How can you call yourselves descendants of Galileo Galilei?!

00:10:02.830 --> 00:10:04.970
May I object?

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:08.460
I don't think my drinking habits are at all relevant to my relation to Galileo...

00:10:08.460 --> 00:10:09.830
Just listen to yourself!

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:14.620
Your morally bankrupt lifestyle taints the great legacy of your ancestor!

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:20.660
Well, isn't it enough that you
inherited his engineering prowess?

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:22.050
I'm going to be a prosecutor.

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.360
As for Kakkii and Hocchii...

00:10:24.890 --> 00:10:28.730
Well, they're both working toward futures of their own.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:33.230
Kidnappers targeted you three for your lack of ambition!

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:34.900
That makes no sense at all.

00:10:34.900 --> 00:10:36.900
Galileo laid the foundations of modern science

00:10:36.900 --> 00:10:40.760
with his discovery of the pendulum's isochronism and the principle of relativity,

00:10:37.590 --> 00:10:40.270
Now Mama's all revved up.

00:10:40.760 --> 00:10:43.030
as well as with his myriad astronomical observations.

00:10:40.840 --> 00:10:43.220
All thanks to Hazu-nee's big mouth.

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:45.770
But above all, his theory of heliocentrism

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:45.080
You're blaming me?

00:10:45.770 --> 00:10:47.570
which upended the prevailing idea of geocentricism—

00:10:47.570 --> 00:10:50.670
Copernicus first proposed that theory, actually.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:52.000
Papa!

00:10:54.750 --> 00:10:57.090
I'm glad you're safe...

00:10:57.710 --> 00:11:00.250
He announced his model in 1543,

00:11:00.250 --> 00:11:03.580
11 years before Galileo was even born.

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:06.010
You're late, Geshio.

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:08.520
Weren't you worried about them?

00:11:08.830 --> 00:11:11.660
I rushed here directly from the lab...

00:11:11.660 --> 00:11:13.690
Why did this happen?

00:11:13.990 --> 00:11:15.200
I understand.

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:18.770
The commonality among them is
they're Galileo's descendants.

00:11:18.770 --> 00:11:20.700
Could that be our lead?

00:11:20.700 --> 00:11:22.380
How is that a motive?

00:11:22.380 --> 00:11:24.950
Who'd see any value in being related to Galileo?

00:11:24.950 --> 00:11:26.200
What did you say?

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.370
Just in case, we'll assign two officers

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:31.660
to take turns watching your home.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:32.940
That won't be enough.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:33.960
Huh?

00:11:33.960 --> 00:11:36.530
I live alone.

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:39.210
And they're separated.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.390
Hurry up and get ready.

00:11:47.530 --> 00:11:49.800
I don't wanna go.

00:11:49.800 --> 00:11:51.390
I don't.

00:11:51.390 --> 00:11:53.900
Oh, it's been a while...

00:11:54.620 --> 00:11:57.230
This place is just as messy as ever.

00:11:57.230 --> 00:11:59.860
It's just organized in its own way.

00:11:59.860 --> 00:12:01.900
I feel sorry for Hozuki.

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:04.480
I think she's adjusted pretty well, actually.

00:12:04.480 --> 00:12:07.160
Kakkii couldn't do it, though.

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:10.950
In any case, Hozuki will be staying with me for a while.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.480
My security is exceptional.

00:12:16.450 --> 00:12:18.680
I'll stay in my lab.

00:13:00.510 --> 00:13:03.220
Sorry, are you hungry?

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:12.930
Picco Rosso, I have to move to Mama's apartment...

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:14.450
What should I do?

00:13:18.330 --> 00:13:20.010
You're starving, huh?

00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:23.490
I'm pretty hungry, too!

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:26.440
Guess I'll have some candy.

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.030
Hazu-nee...

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.120
Yeah?

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.280
What's it like, living alone?

00:13:46.280 --> 00:13:47.880
It's easy.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:51.390
But it can get lonely at times...

00:13:51.930 --> 00:13:54.320
I can forget everything by drinking.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:58.730
And it's not like living here was very fun or anything.

00:14:00.310 --> 00:14:03.040
Maybe I'll leave, too.

00:14:03.040 --> 00:14:05.300
You can't live with me.

00:14:05.300 --> 00:14:07.530
As if I'd want to.

00:14:09.750 --> 00:14:11.030
Need.

00:14:15.290 --> 00:14:16.540
Don't need!

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:18.040
Don't need...

00:14:18.670 --> 00:14:19.760
Need.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.490
<i>Definitely</i> need.

00:14:27.170 --> 00:14:27.970
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:14:28.900 --> 00:14:31.930
You lack even the most basic life skills.

00:14:31.930 --> 00:14:34.840
Anyway, we have to leave as soon as possible.

00:14:35.780 --> 00:14:36.930
Where's Hozuki?

00:14:47.690 --> 00:14:49.490
You should take your time...

00:14:50.180 --> 00:14:51.990
It's your home, isn't it?

00:14:52.390 --> 00:14:54.490
Who the hell are you?

00:14:58.820 --> 00:15:03.000
Italians only have two weaknesses: food and women.

00:15:03.370 --> 00:15:07.970
I can eat goat vomit, and I have no interest in women.

00:15:07.970 --> 00:15:10.920
Thus, I have no weaknesses.

00:15:10.920 --> 00:15:12.010
I'm invincible.

00:15:12.410 --> 00:15:14.510
Why are you after our girls?

00:15:14.910 --> 00:15:18.390
I'll have you raise your hand before you ask any questions.

00:15:20.940 --> 00:15:23.460
Don't they teach you that in school?

00:15:23.460 --> 00:15:26.940
As if I'd want to.

00:15:27.850 --> 00:15:29.440
Make a single move, and I'll shoot.

00:15:29.890 --> 00:15:31.820
Then how can we raise our hands?

00:15:31.820 --> 00:15:33.800
I heard that, girlie.

00:15:33.800 --> 00:15:36.580
The World Cup prelims are tonight, you know?

00:15:36.580 --> 00:15:38.650
So can we just get this over with?

00:15:39.570 --> 00:15:41.580
Where is Galileo's inheritance?

00:15:41.580 --> 00:15:43.200
Inheritance?

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:45.090
I have no idea what you're talking about!

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:48.460
Don't give me that, Madre.

00:15:48.460 --> 00:15:52.090
Would a nice hole in your head help you remember?

00:15:52.090 --> 00:15:53.890
What are you talking about?

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:56.600
There's been some kind of misunderstanding.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:15:58.960
Misunderstanding...

00:15:58.960 --> 00:16:01.480
Misunderstanding, huh?

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:05.980
Salvatore, she said that I'm misunderstanding.

00:16:07.610 --> 00:16:08.530
Don't!

00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:09.720
Huh?

00:16:09.720 --> 00:16:11.030
What was that?

00:16:15.300 --> 00:16:16.980
Kicks hurt, you know?

00:16:16.980 --> 00:16:18.580
Next, it'll be punches.

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:19.740
You!

00:16:20.150 --> 00:16:22.420
Unlawful entry and detention, destruction of property,

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:23.600
illegal possession of firearms and extortion!

00:16:23.600 --> 00:16:25.630
You've been caught red-handed on all counts!

00:16:25.630 --> 00:16:26.710
Huh?

00:16:27.090 --> 00:16:29.590
What's with your slimy attitude?

00:16:29.590 --> 00:16:33.550
You're the biggest scumbag in Italy...

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:35.890
Oh, and you'd definitely make the top three for all of Europe too!

00:16:35.890 --> 00:16:38.490
If there were a World Cup for scumbags,

00:16:38.490 --> 00:16:40.350
you'd totally be in the running!

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.390
Congrats!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.650
Girlie, what's your name?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.370
Hazuki Ferrari!

00:16:48.370 --> 00:16:49.400
Got a problem with it?

00:16:50.180 --> 00:16:51.400
I love it!

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:52.990
Let me call you "Bambina."

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:55.110
I said it's Hazuki Ferrari!

00:16:55.710 --> 00:16:57.620
They're like oil and water...

00:16:57.620 --> 00:17:00.740
The prelims are about to start...

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:02.620
Let's change venues.

00:17:08.620 --> 00:17:11.630
You're all invited to my gorgeous mecha.

00:17:29.660 --> 00:17:30.520
What's that?

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:35.450
Let's go!

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:37.700
I've been waiting for this moment!

00:17:52.090 --> 00:17:53.380
What now?

00:17:53.780 --> 00:17:55.630
It's coming from the basement...

00:17:56.010 --> 00:17:58.130
What the hell is going on?

00:17:58.130 --> 00:18:00.550
Leonardo, what's happening?

00:18:00.550 --> 00:18:01.140
Ow!

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:04.220
Watch it, Giovanni!

00:18:04.220 --> 00:18:05.730
Sorry, Boss.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.480
Get out!

00:18:08.270 --> 00:18:10.020
It isn't loaded.

00:18:11.190 --> 00:18:12.690
Bastard.

00:18:32.500 --> 00:18:33.840
A goldfish?

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.640
It's flying!

00:18:54.870 --> 00:18:56.290
Now what?

00:18:56.990 --> 00:18:58.580
Is that yours?

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.980
It's not mine.

00:18:58.580 --> 00:18:59.980
Not mine.

00:19:01.610 --> 00:19:02.370
Shoot it down!

00:19:06.770 --> 00:19:08.790
Hozuki-chan, take evasive action.

00:19:08.790 --> 00:19:10.040
We'll be hit if you don't.

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:10.960
Eh?

00:19:20.180 --> 00:19:21.090
Gain altitude.

00:19:21.090 --> 00:19:22.260
Altitude!

00:19:22.260 --> 00:19:23.050
Wait!

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.100
No, our home!

00:19:33.730 --> 00:19:34.940
Now I'm angry.

00:19:34.940 --> 00:19:36.230
Let's fight back.

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:54.130
Firing!

00:20:04.900 --> 00:20:07.400
Huh, it's armed?

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:08.810
Cool.

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:13.900
Wanna go head-to-head with my Black Ganymede, Goldfish?

00:20:18.610 --> 00:20:20.030
Locked on...

00:20:20.030 --> 00:20:20.990
Fire!

00:20:28.590 --> 00:20:30.500
Wait, seriously?

00:20:43.420 --> 00:20:45.280
I'm sorry.

00:20:45.280 --> 00:20:47.460
I'll pay for the damage someday.

00:20:47.460 --> 00:20:51.180
They can't hear you until you activate the speakers, Hozuki-chan.

00:20:51.690 --> 00:20:54.010
I'll let you go this once.

00:20:54.010 --> 00:20:56.200
Just this once!

00:20:57.910 --> 00:20:59.570
Later, Bambina.

00:21:00.050 --> 00:21:02.400
I'll press charges one day!

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:05.410
Hozuki?

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:17.160
There you are...

00:21:18.470 --> 00:21:20.490
The three Galileo sisters.

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.110
asa ga kuru no mo kizukanai mama

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:41.110
I used to not even notice the sun rising

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.940
nagareboshi wo sagashiteta

00:21:41.110 --> 00:21:44.940
As I was looking for shooting stars

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:51.950
ano koro no you ni sora wo miageru koto mo shinakunatteta

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:51.950
But now I no longer look up at the sky like that

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:57.080
nande mo nai negaigoto datte

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:57.080
I don't even remember the wishes I wanted to make

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.460
hitori ja nai kono basho nara

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:01.460
That place where I'm not alone

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:06.760
kitto mata mitsukedaseru

00:22:01.460 --> 00:22:06.760
I'm sure I can find it again

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:14.720
ima yozora ni kagayaku hoshikuzu no naka kara

00:22:06.760 --> 00:22:14.720
Among the stardust shining in the night sky

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:23.110
wasurekakete ita itsuka no mirai wo sagasou

00:22:14.720 --> 00:22:23.110
I'll search for the future that I had almost forgotten

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:30.240
me wo korashite hitosuji no hikari ga

00:22:23.110 --> 00:22:30.240
As I strain my eyes to find that single beam of light

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:42.380
oto mo naku nagareru sono kiseki oikakete yukou

00:22:30.240 --> 00:22:42.380
I'll chase after that silently flowing miracle
